      "side": 1,
      "message": "I checked this on Rex. With the current CL (patchset 3), CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_SVDM_RSP is not enabled because it depends on !CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_USB_PD_USB32_DRD, and Rex has CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_USB_PD_USB32_DRD\u003dy. As a result, the common svdm_rsp.c implementation is not linked, and the build succeeds.\n\nAlso tried removing the DRD dependency (patchset 4), which results in CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_SVDM_RSP\u003dy for Rex. The build still succeeded, and I did not see any duplicate implementation or linker errors. Looking at the build logic, usbc_tbt_compat.c is only compiled when both CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_USB_PD_TBT_COMPAT_MODE and CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_USB_PD_ALT_MODE_UFP are enabled. On Rex, CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_USB_PD_ALT_MODE_UFP is not set, so usbc_tbt_compat.c is not included in the build.\n\nBuilt Screebo at this commit, and the build completed successfully.",
      "parentUuid": "a41936d0_fecf53db",
      "revId": "2aaf6ec63d209e00d7689f44f0a4492ada35238b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
